  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 58-year-old man with a prosthetic aortic valve is receiving intravenous vancomycin for MRSA bacteraemia secondary to an infected haemodialysis line. He has stage 5 chronic kidney disease on thrice-weekly haemodialysis. After the loading dose, the unit pharmacist recommends moving from trough-only monitoring to AUC-guided dosing using Bayesian software with two levels per dialysis cycle.',
  'What is the main advantage of AUC-guided vancomycin dosing over trough-only monitoring in this patient?',
  array['vancomycin','AUC monitoring','therapeutic drug monitoring','MRSA bacteraemia']
),
('d7000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'mrcp2', 'fedc0e81-de96-4885-a894-a0f6389f3996',
  'draft', 'advanced',
  $x$A 45-year-old woman with a history of a maculopapular rash after amoxicillin as a child, documented in her records simply as 'penicillin allergy', now requires treatment for streptococcal endocarditis. She has never had penicillin since, and there is no history of anaphylaxis, angioedema, blistering rash or mucosal involvement. The infection prefers a penicillin-based regimen for optimal outcome.$x$,
  'What is the most appropriate next step in managing her reported penicillin allergy?',
  array['penicillin allergy de-labelling','beta-lactam allergy','endocarditis','antimicrobial stewardship']
),
('d7000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', 'mrcp2', 'fedc0e81-de96-4885-a894-a0f6389f3996',
  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 67-year-old man in intensive care with a central venous catheter develops fever and hypotension five days after starting total parenteral nutrition. Blood cultures from both the line and a peripheral site grow Candida albicans. He remains haemodynamically unstable and the central line is removed. Renal function is normal and he is not neutropenic.',
  'Which antifungal regimen is most appropriate as initial therapy?',
  array['candidaemia','echinocandin','antifungal therapy','critical illness']
),
