  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 72-year-old man with a diabetic foot osteomyelitis caused by methicillin-susceptible Staphylococcus aureus has completed two weeks of inpatient intravenous flucloxacillin with good clinical response. He lives alone, has difficult venous access, and there is no local outpatient parenteral antibiotic therapy (OPAT) nursing service available in his area for daily line care.',
  'Which of the following is the most appropriate strategy to complete his antibiotic course?',
