  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 55-year-old man returns from a prolonged hospital admission abroad and develops a urinary tract infection with bacteraemia. Blood culture grows Klebsiella pneumoniae, which on susceptibility testing is resistant to all carbapenems tested, with a positive carbapenemase phenotypic test subsequently confirmed as KPC (Klebsiella pneumoniae carbapenemase) production by molecular testing. He remains septic despite initial broad-spectrum therapy.',
