  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 40-year-old woman with acute myeloid leukaemia on induction chemotherapy develops invasive pulmonary aspergillosis confirmed on CT and galactomannan testing. She is started on voriconazole. Two weeks later, despite adequate oral dosing, her trough level returns unexpectedly low, and she is also newly started on rifampicin for a co-existing mycobacterial infection identified on bronchoalveolar lavage.',
